# The Docker build context (Dockerfile, compose.yaml) holds only what the image is built
# from: everything is ignored except the listed sources, and build outputs inside those
# are ignored again. A local target/, ui/node_modules or ui/build therefore never reaches
# the build, and documentation edits do not invalidate its cached layers.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates/
!vendor/
!ui/
!scripts/build-fmt-wasm.sh
!scripts/docker-healthcheck.sh
!LICENSE
!THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md

**/target
# the Python bindings are their own workspace, outside the root one
crates/sparkles-py
ui/node_modules
ui/build
ui/.svelte-kit
# a local `mise run ui:wasm` build: the image builds its own
ui/src/lib/wasm
# the Playwright tests and their output, and the UI's notes, are not part of the build
ui/tests
ui/test-results
ui/playwright-report
ui/README.md
